course: dictionary
lesson: 7938
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning the writer means by reading the words around it. Those words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: Look at this: «distant reapers». The writer is in the countryside, where cows are cropping the grass and smoke rises from a cottage. So the reapers are people working in far-off fields, cutting a crop.
explain: Now the word changes. The Grim Reaper is a skeleton in a black cloak with a scythe, and he stands for death. Always check: does your meaning fit the sentence? If it does not, try another meaning.
fact: A reaper is a person who cuts and gathers a crop, such as wheat. This meaning is old-fashioned.
fact: A reaper can also be a machine that cuts grain.
fact: «The Grim Reaper» is a picture of death as a skeleton in a black cloak carrying a scythe.
fact: Long ago, reapers cut wheat by hand with sickles and scythes at harvest time.
fact: «You reap what you sow» means your actions bring their own results.
exercise: In the countryside, what are «distant reapers» most likely to be? | A bird singing by the river | Smoke from a cottage chimney | Cows eating the grass | *People cutting a crop in far-off fields
exercise: What does the Grim Reaper stand for? | Rain | A kind farmer | Harvest time | *Death
exercise: Find and copy the word that shows cows are eating the grass. | smoke | *cropping | reads | distant
test: A reaper can be a machine. What does a reaper machine do? | Sings a song | Carries water to the fields | *Cuts grain | Builds stone walls
test: What does «You reap what you sow» mean? | *Your actions bring their own results | You must plant seeds in spring | Farmers always sell their wheat | Death comes for everyone
exam: Jayden says reaper always means death. Why is he wrong? | Reaper is only used in old stories about the Bible | Reapers are always machines | Reaper means a farmer's dog | *A reaper can be a person who cuts a crop or a machine, so the context shows which meaning
